[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zeux/pugixml/issues/529","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zeux/pugixml","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zeux/pugixml/issues/529/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zeux/pugixml/issues/529/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zeux/pugixml/issues/529/events","html_url":"https://github.com/zeux/pugixml/pull/529","id":1432662710,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAEsfpc5CCB4W","number":529,"title":"Add char8_t mode","user":{"login":"gix","id":51795,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxNzk1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51795?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gix","html_url":"https://github.com/gix","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gix/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gix/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gix/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gix/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gix/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gix/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gix/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gix/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gix/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":8,"created_at":"2022-11-02T07:51:21Z","updated_at":"2026-08-24T16:32:36Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zeux/pugixml/pulls/529","html_url":"https://github.com/zeux/pugixml/pull/529","diff_url":"https://github.com/zeux/pugixml/pull/529.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/zeux/pugixml/pull/529.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"### Overview\r\n\r\nThis PR adds a new mode to pugixml which uses C++20 `char8_t` instead of `char` for the UTF-8 interface. I've dubbed it char8 mode and it can be enabled using the `PUGIXML_CHAR8_MODE` option/macro.\r\n\r\n### Motivation\r\n\r\nUsing pugixml in a mixed ANSI/Unicode Windows codebase is quite errorprone. `char` is already used for the system codepage and it can easily happen that a UTF-8-as-char string slips through without conversion. I've found `char8_t` it to be a huge help in migrating stuff to UTF-8.\r\n\r\n### Implementation\r\n\r\nNot much has to be changed. Since pugixml already calls C string functions with UTF-8, we can do the same with `char8_t` by just casting in a few places.\r\n\r\nStream-based methods received an additional overload, since the `char` overload may be used to represent arbitrary bytes, and the `char8_t` overload may be used by string streams.\r\n\r\nAn additional typedef `u8char_t`, which represents the type pugixml uses for a UTF-8 code unit, was added for the conversion functions.\r\n\r\nMost changes had to be done in the test code. Representing raw bytes as string literals does not work for UTF-8 literals, since hex escape codes are interpreted as a Unicode character (and replaced by multiple bytes). Affected places either received a branch with a u8 literal or use a new `RAW()` macro which smuggles in UTF-8 code points using chars.\r\n\r\n### Notes\r\n\r\n- As implemented, the `PUGIXML_CHAR8_MODE` modifies the UTF-8 interface, which means `PUGIXML_WCHAR_MODE` takes precedence if both are defined (no diagnostic).\r\n- I haven't updated the CI build descriptions since I don't know the compiler versions. Locally I've tested with Visual Studio 2022 17.3 and clang 15.\r\n- Maybe an overload taking `char8_t` file paths should be added as well?","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zeux/pugixml/issues/529/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zeux/pugixml/issues/529/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zeux/pugixml/issues/709","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zeux/pugixml","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zeux/pugixml/issues/709/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zeux/pugixml/issues/709/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zeux/pugixml/issues/709/events","html_url":"https://github.com/zeux/pugixml/pull/709","id":4339348770,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAEsfpc7WI6zz","number":709,"title":"cmake: install a fitting config header","user":{"login":"nolange","id":7605849,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2MDU4NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7605849?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nolange","html_url":"https://github.com/nolange","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nolange/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nolange/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nolange/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nolange/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nolange/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nolange/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nolange/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nolange/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nolange/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":2,"created_at":"2026-04-27T22:56:53Z","updated_at":"2026-08-12T21:21:41Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","active_lock_reason":null,"draft":true,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zeux/pugixml/pulls/709","html_url":"https://github.com/zeux/pugixml/pull/709","diff_url":"https://github.com/zeux/pugixml/pull/709.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/zeux/pugixml/pull/709.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"use a header with the correct defines, so\r\nthe defines fit to the compiled library.\r\n\r\nI have to use this when creating a sysroot / sdk for later builds. the options are currently just discarded.\r\n\r\nIdeally the build would use the header too instead of defines, but there is no clean way,\r\nas `#include \"pugiconfig.hpp\"` will pretty consistentely prefer the file next to it.\r\nI could change this to always create from CMake, but I guess that breaks all the other build systems.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zeux/pugixml/issues/709/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zeux/pugixml/issues/709/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zeux/pugixml/issues/734","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zeux/pugixml","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zeux/pugixml/issues/734/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zeux/pugixml/issues/734/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zeux/pugixml/issues/734/events","html_url":"https://github.com/zeux/pugixml/pull/734","id":5135383611,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAEsfpc7-Rxxh","number":734,"title":"cmake: add option to enable std::string_view","user":{"login":"nolange","id":7605849,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc2MDU4NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7605849?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nolange","html_url":"https://github.com/nolange","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nolange/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nolange/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nolange/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nolange/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nolange/subscriptions"